WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.281
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.581 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:20.418
Unit fourteen: Writing Task 2: Essay Structure and Task Response. Today you will plan and structure a 250-word essay that answers the question fully.

4
00:00:20.718 --> 00:00:23.347
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.486
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.456
Introduction.

7
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.844
Introduction means the opening paragraph.

8
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.136
Write a short introduction.

9
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.344
Your turn. Say: Introduction.

10
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.294
Introduction.

11
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.005
Thesis.

12
00:00:45.017 --> 00:00:47.713
Thesis means your clear position on the question.

13
00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:50.339
State your thesis in the introduction.

14
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.405
Your turn. Say: Thesis.

15
00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.279
Thesis.

16
00:00:58.017 --> 00:00:59.354
Body paragraph.

17
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.987
Body paragraph means a paragraph that develops one main idea.

18
00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:06.397
Write two body paragraphs.

19
00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:09.694
Your turn. Say: Body paragraph.

20
00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:14.219
Body paragraph.

21
00:01:14.983 --> 00:01:15.984
Conclusion.

22
00:01:16.983 --> 00:01:19.192
Conclusion means the final paragraph.

23
00:01:19.783 --> 00:01:21.481
Summarise in the conclusion.

24
00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:25.026
Your turn. Say: Conclusion.

25
00:01:27.867 --> 00:01:28.949
Conclusion.

26
00:01:29.683 --> 00:01:31.010
Task response.

27
00:01:32.017 --> 00:01:35.003
Task response means how fully you answer the question.

28
00:01:35.617 --> 00:01:38.034
Task Response is a marking criterion.

29
00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:41.209
Your turn. Say: Task response.

30
00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:45.381
Task response.

31
00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:46.920
Argument.

32
00:01:47.917 --> 00:01:50.323
Argument means a reason supporting a view.

33
00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:52.452
Support each argument.

34
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.795
Your turn. Say: Argument.

35
00:01:58.633 --> 00:01:59.623
Argument.

36
00:02:00.383 --> 00:02:01.396
Example.

37
00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:05.555
Example means a specific case that supports an idea.

38
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.627
Add a clear example.

39
00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:10.973
Your turn. Say: Example.

40
00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:14.800
Example.

41
00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:16.458
Relevant.

42
00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.612
Relevant means connected to the question.

43
00:02:20.217 --> 00:02:21.671
Keep ideas relevant.

44
00:02:22.283 --> 00:02:24.878
Your turn. Say: Relevant.

45
00:02:27.733 --> 00:02:28.700
Relevant.

46
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.837
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:33.683 --> 00:02:36.194
Visal, how long is Writing Task 2?

48
00:02:37.283 --> 00:02:46.472
You write at least 250 words in about forty minutes. Task 2 carries more marks than Task 1, so plan your time carefully.

49
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:49.188
What is a good structure?

50
00:02:50.283 --> 00:03:00.703
Use four paragraphs: introduction, two body paragraphs and a conclusion. In the introduction, paraphrase the question and give your position.

51
00:03:01.817 --> 00:03:03.689
What does Task Response mean?

52
00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:15.899
It means you answer every part of the question, give a clear position and support each idea with reasons and examples. Off-topic ideas lose marks.

53
00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:18.336
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:19.183 --> 00:03:23.017
Grammar focus: Strategy: plan, write, check.

55
00:03:23.317 --> 00:03:24.504
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:25.217 --> 00:03:28.505
The introduction paraphrases the question and gives my position.

57
00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:33.285
Each body paragraph has one main idea with a reason and an example.

58
00:03:34.233 --> 00:03:42.400
Spend five minutes planning. Answer every part of the question, keep to one main idea per paragraph, and leave two minutes to check your work.

59
00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:46.812
Be careful! Don't say: I start writing without a plan.

60
00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:51.556
Say: I plan for five minutes first.

61
00:03:51.856 --> 00:03:53.193
Plan before writing.

62
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.757
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:58.881
Planning an Essay.

64
00:03:59.181 --> 00:04:02.458
The question asks whether students should wear uniforms.

65
00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:06.140
Lina spends five minutes writing a plan.

66
00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:10.921
In the introduction she paraphrases the question and states her view.

67
00:04:11.933 --> 00:04:15.280
Each body paragraph develops one reason with an example.

68
00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:20.310
In the conclusion she summarises her position without new ideas.

69
00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.564
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:26.417 --> 00:04:28.927
How many words are required in Task 2?

71
00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:34.250
A, 150. B, 400. C, 250.

72
00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.392
The answer is C: 250.

73
00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.224
The introduction should blank.

74
00:04:43.524 --> 00:04:48.095
A, state your position. B, give new examples. C, end the essay.

75
00:04:51.633 --> 00:04:54.086
The answer is A: state your position.

76
00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.923
Each body paragraph has blank main idea.

77
00:04:58.223 --> 00:05:01.563
A, no. B, one. C, five.

78
00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.891
The answer is B: one.

79
00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:09.991
Task Response means blank.

80
00:05:10.291 --> 00:05:15.721
A, using long words. B, writing fast. C, answering the whole question.

81
00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:22.183
The answer is C: answering the whole question.

82
00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:24.862
How long does Lina plan?

83
00:05:25.162 --> 00:05:29.407
A, five minutes. B, twenty minutes. C, one minute.

84
00:05:32.967 --> 00:05:35.303
The answer is A: five minutes.

85
00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:40.232
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:41.083 --> 00:05:43.153
How do you structure a Task 2 essay?

87
00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.508
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:53.808 --> 00:06:12.450
I plan for five minutes and then write four paragraphs. The introduction paraphrases the question and states my position, and each body paragraph develops one idea with a reason and an example. The conclusion summarises my view without adding new ideas.

89
00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.390
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:15.283 --> 00:06:20.478
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: plan, write, check.

91
00:06:20.778 --> 00:06:25.242
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:06:25.542 --> 00:06:28.241
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:28.541 --> 00:06:31.913
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

